The test’s `ax.legend(...)` call passes `bbox_to_anchor=(0.98, 0.95)`. In `Legend.__init__`, that argument is passed directly into `set_bbox_to_anchor`. In `Legend.set_bbox_to_anchor`, non-`BboxBase` inputs are checked by length, and when the tuple length is 2 the method rewrites it as `[bbox[0], bbox[1], 0, 0]` before calling `Bbox.from_bounds(*bbox)`. Substituting the test values gives left `0.98`, bottom `0.95`, width `0.0`, height `0.0`.

## Answer
{"bottom":0.95,"height":0.0,"left":0.98,"width":0.0}
